<section class="method-section" id="time-difference" aria-labelledby="time-diff-heading">
  <div class="method-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Time Difference Mechanics</p>
    <h2 id="time-diff-heading">Understanding the +10 Hour Gap: GMT to AEST</h2>
    <p>
      The time difference between Greenwich Mean Time (GMT) and Australian Eastern Standard Time (AEST) is exactly <strong>10 hours</strong>. Since GMT is fixed at UTC+0 and AEST operates at UTC+10, Eastern Australia sits ten hours ahead of the meridian baseline. When it is 8:00 AM in London during winter, the clocks in Sydney, Melbourne, and Brisbane show 6:00 PM local time.
    </p>
    <p>
      However, the calculation shifts when daylight saving rules apply. The United Kingdom and southeastern Australia observe daylight saving time on opposite cycles because they are located in different hemispheres. When the UK switches to British Summer Time (BST, UTC+1), the gap between London and Brisbane narrows to 9 hours. Conversely, when southeastern Australia shifts to Australian Eastern Daylight Time (AEDT, UTC+11), Sydney and Melbourne run 11 hours ahead of GMT. 
    </p>
  </div>

  <!-- Custom GMT vs AEST Infographic (SVG) -->
  <div style="margin: 2rem auto; max-width: 700px; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 12px;">
