  <div class="method-grid">
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>GMT Standard Zero</h3>
      <p>Greenwich Mean Time is the baseline (UTC+0) and remains unchanged throughout the year. It does not observe daylight saving shifts, making it the anchor point for all offset math.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>AEST standard (+10)</h3>
      <p>Australian Eastern Standard Time runs at UTC+10. It is observed in Brisbane year-round and is the standard winter time for Sydney, Melbourne, Hobart, and Canberra.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="method-card">
      <h3>AEDT Summer Shift (+11)</h3>
      <p>From October to April, southeastern states change to AEDT (UTC+11). During this period, the timezone gap between London and Sydney increases to 11 hours, while Brisbane remains at +10.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

